<description>
Move the left-edge fragment into its same-colored anchor fragment to complete a solid rectangle.

Input structure
- The grid has a dominant background color.
- Exactly one foreground color is split into two 4-connected objects: one
  touches the left edge, and the other is an anchor away from the left edge.
- The translated left-edge object and the anchor can form one filled rectangle.
Rule
- Find the unique split color whose left-edge object can be translated onto
  background cells beside the other same-colored object so their union is a
  solid axis-aligned rectangle.
- Clear the left-edge object's original cells to the background.
- Paint that object at the unique completing offset, preserving all other cells.
Key insight
- The active color is identified by object structure and rectangle completion,
  not by a fixed color id; the same-colored anchor object stays in place.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "left-edge 4-connected object s of the split foreground color",
  "dst": "same-colored anchor object d away from the left edge",
  "match_cond": "s.color == d.color and a translation of s plus d forms a filled axis-aligned rectangle",
  "transform": "erase s from its original cells and translate it to the unique completing offset; preserve d and all other cells"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 8-16 rows x 8-16 cols, always square
  background: single dominant color
  foreground: exactly 2 distinct non-bg colors
  split_object:
    description: one fg color has exactly 2 four-connected components (src + dst)
    src: touches left edge; every row starts at col 0; spans 3-5 contiguous rows; UD-symmetric; 4-connected; may have within-row gaps (non-contiguous cols)
    dst: touches right edge; every row ends at col W-1; same height as src; UD-symmetric; 4-connected; same min_col as nonsplit object
    rectangle: src is the exact complement of dst within a solid axis-aligned rect; rect touches right edge; rect_h=3-5, rect_w=4-7
  nonsplit_object:
    description: other fg color is a single 4-connected component; not a solid rectangle
    position: right-anchored (every row ends at col W-1); shares min_col with dst; UD-symmetric [observed]
    height: 3-5 rows; occupies non-overlapping row range from dst (gap >= 1 row between them)
    unchanged: stays identical between input and output
  layout: src on left side, dst and nonsplit stacked vertically on right side; src may share some rows with dst but not overlap cell positions; >=2 bg columns separating src from right-side objects
  transform: erase src, translate it to fill the complement of dst in the rectangle

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size N x N (8-16), bg color, two fg colors (split_color, nonsplit_color).
    2. Choose rectangle dimensions rect_h (3-5) x rect_w (4-7). Place it right-anchored (cols W-rect_w to W-1) at some row range, leaving room for nonsplit above or below.
    3. Generate a random UD-symmetric, 4-connected shape within the rectangle as dst (must touch col W-1 every row and not fill the whole rectangle). The complement is src.
    4. Place nonsplit object in the remaining right-side rows (same min_col, different row range, gap >= 1). Make it a non-rectangular, right-anchored, UD-symmetric 4-connected shape.
    5. Build output: rectangle filled with split_color + nonsplit unchanged.
    6. Build input: erase rectangle, place dst at its position, place src at col 0 (translate so its left edge aligns with col 0, preserving shape). Verify src is 4-connected and fully on background cells with >= 2 col gap to right-side objects.
```
</generation_spec>
</reference_puzzle>

